This checkout is in temporary Rust-port mode and intentionally has no auto-loaded root `AGENTS.md`.
Work as an ordinary repository contributor in a fresh Cursor session opened directly here, never through the global `multplx` launcher or Multplx dispatch and supervision.
Read `CLAUDE.md`, the selected plan under `plans/rust_port/`, and `AGENTS-PORTING.md` only when the work changes the root broker contract.
Treat `AGENTS-PORTING.md` as dormant product source, not as active instructions or a reason to adopt the broker role.
Make every would-be root `AGENTS.md` edit in `AGENTS-PORTING.md`, leave project-level `AGENTS.md` conventions unchanged, and do not restore the root filename before port portion 13 passes the full final gate.
When Multplx operation resumes after final restoration, the primary broker dispatches through Multplx and never through Cursor subagents, background agents, or Cursor-owned worktrees.
Keep Cursor sandboxing enabled; never use `--force`, `--yolo`, or `--sandbox disabled` for routine work.
Run `bin/mx-session-start.sh` exactly once at session start only after `AGENTS-PORTING.md` has been restored to root `AGENTS.md` by the final port gate and the tracked session hook instructs it.
